<title>GERMANY: INTERVIEW-Buba's Welteke sure of timely EMU start.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW-Buba's Welteke sure of timely EMU start.</headline>
<byline>Kate Kelland</byline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Ernst Welteke said on Tuesday he was certain that Europe's single currency project would start on time in January 1999.</p>
<p>In an interview with Reuters, Welteke, who is also president of state central bank in Hesse, applauded the progress of European convergence and warned against delaying economic and monetary union (EMU), saying such a move would wreak havoc on the German economy.</p>
</text>
